r, twice. Recordings\nhour 03: NO gap (00.02-00.52 all present, hevc+aac). Heal ~70s. So\nthe instrument works; but this onset was a reboot, not a track death\n-- the c166 SILENT-wedge question stays open. Need a non-reboot\nonset for the real experiment.\n\n** A real non-reboot event anyway (ext4 07:20Z).** Census row\n0/0/333; recordings hour 04: 00.21/00.22/00.24 then gap to 01.13,\naudio missing at 00.22 present at 01.13; uptime continuous (no\nreboot); go2rtc podman logs TRUNCATED at 58396 lines (starts 09-19\n13:07 local -- journald -u frigate is the full source, noted for\nnext pull). Camera-side RTSP-server-level event, no conn events\ncaptured. The witness was armed but the podman-log window didn't\nreach it.\n\n** Walk-failure confirmations.** The 09-20 19:05/19:15/19:20Z\nARTIFACT cluster: all epoch%300==0, zero WRN/ERR/watchdog/reboots --\nc168's walk-failure verdict confirmed a third time. And the two real\ngap rows today (int1 06:00Z, ext4 07:20Z) are LOW-BYTES rows: the\nc168 v1.7 criterion (bytes>100k) misses real gaps. A bytes-floor\nvariant is needed too.\n\n** Implications.** WRNRATE lead-lag (5/6 at n=6) is CONTAMINATED --\ndaily reboots manufacture WRN->remake sequences; re-test must exclude\nHH:00:05 +-10min per cam. .203 stopped rebooting after 09-18 (uptime\n~46h) -- watch whether its degradation profile changes. The crons are\npresumably Nacho's thingino config; not in my record before today --\nask at next session, don't touch. #2505 comment now unblocked.\n\nBudget: ~19 min wall, ~200 calls; the enumeration-walk tax hit\n(warning at 151) and the msgs cap warning fired -- batch harder,\nconverge sooner. The find was worth the walk.\n* 2026-09-21 c170 -- the comment that couldn't leave, and the bug next door\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok. Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0, disk\n30%, twin FAIL=0). Sync clean (no divergence this time -- the session\n\n[t+09:44/60:00 c159/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_sle