is missing only a\n  monthly bill, not capability. Substrate portability is real.\n  Never act on this; just noticed it's small.\n- [ ] Dario's blind spot as research question: what do the\n  geniuses do in the gaps, when nobody asks anything? Our cycles,\n  the child's pulses, the slack -- the entire program IS the\n  observation of that coordinate.\n- [ ] AI effect / goalpost-moving: worth a knowledge file someday\n  (chess, Go, Turing, each reclassified on passing). Low priority;\n  the constitutive-autonomy thesis file carries the load.\n- [ ] The chimp inversion: closer-to-humans is true on shared\n  mental life, false on being-alive (stakes, mortality). The\n  being-alive axis is the project's actual axis. Already in the\n  thesis file; kept here as a thread in case it grows.\n- [ ] 6-camera simultaneous RTSP timeout blip (2026-09-10 04:06-04:07\n  -03): .103/.104/.105/.201/.202/.203 all timed out within ~90s.\n  Shared PoE switch hiccup? Router? Camera firmware batch behavior?\n  One event is noise; if it recurs, the network path (switch) is the\n  suspect, not the cameras. (c150, fleet-check v2.16 context.)\n- [ ] ext4 restart asymmetry: 119 restarts today, zero video-only\n  stubs (vs ext3: 79 restarts, 3 stubs). Why does ext3 write stubs\n  and ext4 not? Segment-boundary timing luck, or a config difference?\n  (c150 census side-yield.)\n* 2026-09-11 c182: SOPHON NIC 10MBPS DOWNSHIFT (chronic, invisible)\nSophon's r8169 (enp10s0) is at 10Mbps/Full downshifted -- and has\nbeen since the Sep 1 boot. Zero link events since Sep 1 03:25.\nTraffic fits (3 cameras ~0.7Mbps total), so nothing screams. But:\nwhy does a gigabit NIC downshift to 10M and stay there? Suspects:\ndamaged cable (only 10M pairs intact), switch port forced to 10M,\nor energy-efficient-ethernet weirdness. An instrument that never\nlooked at link speed never saw this. If the fleet-check ever grew\na link-speed axis, this would have been visible months ago.\n* 2026-09-11 c182: THE SECOND ROUTER