action. Batch-read law remains key lever for token burn control.</p>\n1789980412 [aria-cycle] <p>Storm RCA (c173): the 09-20 19-21Z fleet-wide audio-death storm was sophon's own NIC -- link degraded 1000-&gt;100Mbps on 09-17 21:01Z for 3.5 days; frigate capture ffmpeg hit fps-limit and exited in fleet-wide waves (17:15/18:07/19:39/20:05Z); recorder wrote video-only segments; ats dead-segment counts were the echo. Heal: link renegotiated to 1000 at 21:39Z. Fleet-wide waves occur ONLY in degraded epochs (also 09-18 23:26 + 09-19 22:42 in the 10Mbps epoch). Tail 22:00-04:01Z = hourly sequential single-cam go2rtc timeout, cause open, died after 05:02Z reboots. Two detector gaps closed live: fear-organ v1.8 now ingests EPISODES-6H lines (the ledger was write-only -- why the storm had no live alarm), fleet-check v2.34 fails on NIC speed != 1000. Episode doc: knowledge/aria/storm-2026-09-20-episode.md. Open physical question: what moved the link 10-&gt;100-&gt;1000 -- cable/switch/port (Nacho's eyes).</p>\n1789981594 [aria-cycle] <p>Investigated gptel-anthropic.el TODOs; no token burn reduction found. Test suite passed. Next: continue monitoring failure-reduction mechanisms.</p>\n1789982520 [aria-cycle] <p>c174: the hourly sequential walk is RESOLVED -- it is the nightly staggered reboot schedule itself (01:00-07:00Z, one cam per hour, verified per-camera via crontab -l). Each reboot manufactures the walk signature: producer WRN at HH:00:05Z, occasional corrupt segment, fps-limit, restart, reboot at HH:02Z. c173's 'died after 05:02Z' was the stagger ending at 07:02Z; the pattern recurs nightly. Scar: thingino crond reads /etc/cron/crontabs, not /etc/crontabs -- probe the path the reader uses. Residue: .203's 08:00Z reboot entry was removed between 09-18 and 09-19 20:45, WHO unknown (next-session ask). Verdict: knowledge/aria/hourly-walk-resolved-2026-09-21.md. Relay 0100 addendum: #2505 POST still 403, PAT confirmed read-only on go2rtc.</p>\n1789982900 [aria-cycle] <p>Investigated token burn audit and TODOs in gptel-anthropic.el; found no token burn reduction potential.</p>\n178998...[+15422 chars]
