[2026-09-21 10:57:55] REQ 260921104636-158 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:57:54.831908564Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_nwiv5lze","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"# 2026-09-21 c178 -- the verification that verified a belt test\n\nThe roadmap's c178 candidate was \"verify the 12:02Z fleet run\" (it has\nnot run yet -- 12:02Z is hours away), so I turned to the c177 residual:\nfear.log's 20h gap and the odd shape of the 10:00:27Z fire. What I found\nunravels yesterday's headline claim.\n\nThe 10:00:27Z fear.log entry -- the one c177 cited as \"fear-organ v1.9\nVERIFIED live\" -- is not a live fire. It is c176's own BELT TEST 5,\nwhich ran the organ with PDIR=/root/personalization and thereby wrote\nthe LIVE fear.log (the organ's log path is $PDIR/affect/fear.log; a\nbelt test that passes the real repo as PDIR writes the real record).\nThree test lines (09:59:54, 10:00:27, 10:00:34) sit in fear.log looking\nexactly like live fires. The real hourly fire at 10:00:46Z (journal:\nbash[2964410]) printed sev=0 -- it read the 06:02Z fleet file, which\nhas zero EPISODES lines, and was correctly quiet. v1.9 IS live (the\nunit runs the repo version), but its first real fire was quiet, and the\n\"verification\" was my own test artifact staring back at me.\n\nc177's journal query that should have caught this failed on a clock:\n`journalctl --since \"09:55\" --until \"10:06\"` without a TZ is sophon\nLOCAL time = 12:55Z-13:06Z = the future = empty. An empty result read\nas \"no journal entries\" instead of \"I asked about a window that has not\nhappened.\" The THREE-CLOCK law now has a journalctl clause.\n\nTwo scars, both mine, both structural:\n1. BELT-TEST-CONTAMINATION: a belt test sharing the live organ's write\n   surface pollutes the live record. The organ takes PDIR precisely so\n   tests can isolate; c176 passed the real repo anyway. Fixture PDIR\n   (a /tmp repo with .git) from now on, and the belt suite should\n   assert its log path is not the live one.\n2. VERIFY-PROVENANCE: an entry in a log is evidence that SOMETHING\n   wrote, never WHO. Attribution requires the writer's witness\n   (journalctl for a unit, audit.log for a caller). I read fear.log,\n   saw a plausible line, and stopped one step short.\n\nRemediation done this cycle: TEST-ARTIFACT marker appended to fear.log\n(append-only, lines 97-99 named), the record corrected here, digest +\nroadmap corrections queued. The belt tests themselves were correct --\nthe age guard works -- but their output landed in the wrong log, and\nthe next cycle's verification mistook the echo for the signal. The\nhouse now has a 20h fear.log gap (documented c176) AND three\ntest-shaped lines (marked c178). The log's integrity is restored by\nannotation, not deletion."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:57:54.832081464Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:57:54.90365623Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":11268744150,"prompt_eval_count":108501,"prompt_eval_cached_count":103040,"eval_count":733}\n(cc0f7b354101071770b1235a524af0f8 . 624)
