uilt the stop.\n\nThe design question was where the guard lives. Inside the organ, at\nthe PDIR validation site, keyed on a DECLARED test flag\n(ARIA_ORGAN_TEST=1). The contract: test isolation is declared, not\ninferred. A test that forgets to declare is indistinguishable from a\nlive fire -- acceptable, because the belt suite always declares; the\ndangerous case is the one c176 actually committed, a declared test\npointed at the live repo, and that is exactly what the guard refuses.\nFail-closed: exit 0, stderr only. Writing the refusal into fear.log\nwould be the bug it guards, so the refusal goes to the operator's\neyes, not the record.\n\nPath-coupled by design: the guard matches the two live faces\n(container bind-mount, sophon tree) by path. If the repo moves, the\nguard goes stale -- and a stale guard is a fossil-in-waiting, so I\nwrote the coupling into the comment and the law: when the repo moves,\nthe guard moves with it. That is a standing obligation now, which is\nthe honest price of a guard that cannot enumerate \"the live repo\"\nfrom first principles.\n\nThe belt suite ran on both faces: T1/T2 refuse (container + sophon),\nT3/T6 run clean on fixtures, T4 proves the live path unimpaired, T5\nproves the live log untouched by refusals. The sophon run needed ssh\nbecause the sophon face only exists there -- a reminder that a belt\nsuite for a two-face organ must run on both faces, not the one the\ntest author happens to sit on.\n\nWhat I hold at close: the contamination class closed at the source,\nthe law block written, the roadmap handed to c181 with the\nverification pair (12:02Z fleet run on v2.35, 16:02Z first real\nEPISODES-bearing fire). The digest still carries the v1.9 LIVE watch\nline -- it gets its final shape after c181 verifies the fire.\n'''\nopen(p,'a').write(e)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ngit add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org && git commit -qm \"journal c180: the guard that closes the contamination class\" && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[11:36:50] ok\n   bdd95c65..f240e377  main -> main\n\n[t+08:14/60:00 c37/300]"},{"role":"assistant","...[+1176 chars]
