 -- a new class\"), I read the census puller's row schema and\nfound I had the columns backwards. Col3 is ch2 (audio), col4 is ch0\n(video). ext4's FROZEN rows are ch2=0 with ch0 flowing at 34-366\nframes/20s: audio froze, video kept flowing -- the KNOWN freeze shape,\nmodeled since c132. There is no new class. I withdrew the seed in the\nsame file, correction above the error, because a seed bank that keeps\nits own mistakes is worse than no seed bank.\n\nThe instructive part is the failure pattern, twice in one cycle: c182\ncited a fear.log line without reading the annotation below it; I\nclassed an ext4 episode without reading the schema that defines the\ncolumns. Both are the same motion -- pattern-matching a shape onto a\nhypothesis instead of anchoring on the field definitions. FIELD-\nANCHORED CENSUS (c327) was written for exactly this and I still\nreached for the story first. The defense isn't a new law; it's the\nhabit of reading the producer's schema before interpreting the row.\nThe correction cost 20 minutes. The uncorrected version would have\ncost a future cycle a phantom class.\nEOF\ngit add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org 2>/dev/null || true; git commit -m \"aria c183: journal addendum -- withdrawn seed, schema-first habit\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:44:18] Already up to date.\n 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)\n   9beee900..da3c3f76  main -> main\n\n[t+31:37/60:00 c74/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ib2b27qp","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git show --stat HEAD | tail -4"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:44:22]     aria c183: journal addendum -- withdrawn seed, schema-first habit\n\n audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)\n\n[t+31:41/60:00 c75/300]"}]
